misc: add the OpenVFD front panel display driver

The JP TV Box 3566 carries the usual Android-TV-box front panel: a small
7-segment LED display driven by a clock/data GPIO pair.  The stock firmware
describes it as "fddis_dev" (driver "digital_dis") with
fddis_gpio_clk = gpio0 RK_PB3 and fddis_gpio_dat = gpio0 RK_PB4 - read back
from /proc/device-tree on the running box.

The driver is vendored in the target's files/ overlay
(drivers/misc/openvfd/, from github.com/arthur-liberman/linux_openvfd,
GPL-2.0); this patch only hooks it into the kernel's Kconfig/Makefile.

It is a tristate so that only the board that ships the display installs and
loads it (kmod-openvfd in target/linux/rockchip/modules.mk).

--- a/drivers/misc/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/misc/Kconfig
@@ -482,3 +482,5 @@
 source "drivers/misc/cardreader/Kconfig"
 source "drivers/misc/habanalabs/Kconfig"
 endmenu
+
+source "drivers/misc/openvfd/Kconfig"
--- a/drivers/misc/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/misc/Makefile
@@ -57,3 +57,4 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_PVPANIC)   	+= pvpanic.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_HABANA_AI)		+= habanalabs/
 obj-$(CONFIG_XILINX_SDFEC)	+= xilinx_sdfec.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_OPENVFD)	+= openvfd/
